## 3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD, with the partition the body induces on each lvalue (7n-5)

Guard (the deleted predicate) reads:  size, scaledness.
Body (what the 24 cells run after the deletion: main :259-262 printf + print_function_name(size, store, signedness,
endianness, scaledness, usr, registeroffset, no_pc_sync)) reads all eight loop variables.  Partitions it induces:
  size          tested == 0 (with endianness, :74) and > 0 (with scaledness, :80); otherwise only PRINTED (1 << size,
                :69).  Body-tested partition {0} | {1,2,3}; the printed width distinguishes every value.
  scaledness    truthy at :80                      {0} | {32}
  store         truthy at :62                      {0} | {4}
  signedness    truthy at :66, only when !store    {0} | {8}
  endianness    :71 (>= 0, always true from main), :74 (with size == 0), :77 truthy   {0} | {16}, collapsed for size 0
  usr           truthy at :83                      {0} | {64}
  registeroffset truthy at :86                     {0} | {128}
  no_pc_sync    truthy at :89                      {0} | {256}
Body-only fields: store, signedness, endianness, usr, registeroffset, no_pc_sync.  All eight are written ONLY by the
nested for-loop headers of main() (:221-234), independently, and the loops enumerate the whole product -- so every
state where a body-only field "disagrees" with the guard occurs.  Inside the guard cell (size == 0 && scaledness) the
dominating arms fix registeroffset = 128 (arm C) and exclude store && signedness (arm A), leaving
{ld.bu, ld.b, st.b} x endianness{0,16} x usr{0,64} x no_pc_sync{0,256} = 24 cells -- EXHAUSTED by A6's 24 pins.
No disagreeing-state row is owed beyond them.
Which pins hold which cell outside the guard (the accept side, B3):
  size 1, scaled     161 (LE), 177 (BE): ld.hu regofs sync -- the D2 B+1 edge of :80 (B-1 is size -1, outside the
                     domain; codex :148).  EXHAUSTED for the edge compare (its two endian cells); other halfword kinds
                     SAMPLED (ld.h/st.h, .usr, nopcsync not rowed).
  size 2, scaled     418/422 (LE), 434/438 (BE): xmem word ld/st, nopcsync -- SAMPLED.
  size 3, scaled     NOT ROWED (doubleword; Grok :91 "the far value") -- clause (e), disclosed.
  size 0, unscaled   144, 400, 404 + the 21 cparts = all 24 regofs unscaled byte cells -- EXHAUSTED for the guard's
                     scaledness = 0 region at size 0, registeroffset 128.  The unscaled byte cells with
                     registeroffset 0 (the immediate forms, indices 0..127 / 256..383) are NOT rowed -- SAMPLED none,
                     clause (e).

